{"id":"mahabharata-8-038","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":38,"title":"अष्टात्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 38 · Dhrishtadyumna against the Kaurava chiefs","summary":{"en":"Kritavarman, Kripa, Drona's son, Karna, Uluka and Shakuni attack the Pandava chiefs, and Duryodhana faces Nakula and Sahadeva. Dhrishtadyumna's head is nearly struck off, and the Kauravas rush at him in a body.","kn":"ಕೃತವರ್ಮ, ಕೃಪ, ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮ, ಕರ್ಣ, ಉಲೂಕ, ಶಕುನಿ ಪಾಂಡವ ನಾಯಕರ ಮೇಲೆ ಎರಗುತ್ತಾರೆ; ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ನಕುಲ-ಸಹದೇವರನ್ನು ಎದುರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಧೃಷ್ಟದ್ಯುಮ್ನನ ತಲೆ ಬಹುತೇಕ ಕಡಿಯಲ್ಪಡುತ್ತದೆ; ಕೌರವರು ಒಟ್ಟಾಗಿ ಅವನ ಮೇಲೆ ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"कृतवर्मा, कृप, अश्वत्थामा, कर्ण, उलूक और शकुनि पाण्डव नायकों पर आक्रमण करते हैं, और दुर्योधन नकुल-सहदेव का सामना करता है। धृष्टद्युम्न का सिर लगभग कटने को होता है, और कौरव मिलकर उस पर टूट पड़ते हैं।","te":"కృతవర్మ, కృపుడు, అశ్వత్థామ, కర్ణుడు, ఉలూకుడు, శకుని పాండవ నాయకులపై దాడి చేస్తారు; దుర్యోధనుడు నకుల సహదేవులను ఎదుర్కొంటాడు. ధృష్టద్యుమ్నుని తల దాదాపు తెగిపోతుంది; కౌరవులు గుంపుగా అతనిపై దూకుతారు.","ta":"கிருதவர்மன், கிருபர், அஸ்வத்தாமன், கர்ணன், உலூகன், சகுனி பாண்டவத் தலைவரைத் தாக்க, துரியோதனன் நகுல சகதேவரை எதிர்க்கிறான். த்ருஷ்டத்யும்னனின் தலை கிட்டத்தட்ட வெட்டப்பட, கௌரவர் கூட்டமாக அவன்மேல் பாய்கின்றனர்.","ml":"കൃതവർമ്മാവ്, കൃപർ, ദ്രോണപുത്രൻ, കർണ്ണൻ, ഉലൂകൻ, ശകുനി എന്നിവർ പാണ്ഡവനായകന്മാരെ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു; ദുര്യോധനൻ നകുലനെയും സഹദേവനെയും നേരിടുന്നു. ധൃഷ്ടദ്യുമ്നന്റെ തല ഏറെക്കുറെ അറ്റുപോകുന്നു; കൗരവർ കൂട്ടമായി അദ്ദേഹത്തിനു നേരെ പായുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.38; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कृतवर्मा कृपो द्रौणिः सूतपुत्रश्च मारिष ।\nउलूकः सौबलश्चैव राजा च सह सोदरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord, Kritavarma, Kripa, Ashvatthama, the charioteer's son Karna, Uluka, Shakuni son of Subala, and King Duryodhana with his brothers saw the army sinking, tormented by fear of the sons of Pandu."}},{"n":2,"text":"सीदमानां चमूं दृष्ट्वा पाण्डुपुत्रभयार्दिताम् ।\nसमुज्जिहीर्षुर्वेगेन भिन्नां नावमिवार्णवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"They wished to lift it up quickly, like a broken ship in the ocean."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततो युद्धमतीवासीन्मुहूर्तमिव भारत ।\nभीरूणां त्रासजननं शूराणां हर्षवर्धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, then a fierce battle began that lasted a short while, bringing terror to cowards and delight to heroes."}},{"n":4,"text":"कृपेण शरवर्षाणि विप्रमुक्तानि संयुगे ।\nसृञ्जयाः शातयामासुः शलभानां व्रजा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Srinjayas cut down the showers of arrows that Kripa loosed in the battle, as if they were swarms of locusts."}},{"n":5,"text":"शिखण्डी तु ततः क्रुद्धो गौतमं त्वरितो ययौ ।\nववर्ष शरवर्षाणि समन्तादेव ब्राह्मणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shikhandi, angry, swiftly went against Kripa, son of Gautama, and rained showers of arrows on the brahmin from every side."}},{"n":6,"text":"कृपस्तु शरवर्षं तद्विनिहत्य महास्त्रवित् ।\nशिखण्डिनं रणे क्रुद्धो विव्याध दशभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Kripa, skilled in great weapons, struck down that shower of arrows and in anger pierced Shikhandi in the battle with ten arrows."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततः शिखण्डी कुपीतः शरैः सप्तभिराहवे ।\nकृपं विव्याध सुभृशं कङ्कपत्रैरजिह्मगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shikhandi, enraged, pierced Kripa hard in the fight with seven straight-flying arrows with heron feathers."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततः कृपः शरैस्तीक्ष्णैः सोऽतिविद्धो महारथः ।\nव्यश्वसूतरथं चक्रे पार्षतं तु द्विजोत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kripa, the great chariot-warrior and best of brahmins, badly wounded, then with sharp arrows left the son of Prishata without horses, charioteer or chariot."}},{"n":9,"text":"हताश्वात्तु ततो यानादवप्लुत्य महारथः ।\nचर्मखड्गे च संगृह्य सत्वरं ब्राह्मणं ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great chariot-warrior jumped down from his chariot whose horses were slain, took up shield and sword, and went swiftly at the brahmin."}},{"n":10,"text":"तमापतन्तं सहसा शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ।\nछादयामास समरे तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Shikhandi rushed on him suddenly, Kripa covered him in the battle with arrows with bent joints, and it was a marvel."}},{"n":11,"text":"तत्राद्भुतमपश्याम शिलानां प्लवनं यथा ।\nनिश्चेष्टो यद्रणे राजञ्शिखण्डी समतिष्ठत ॥","meaning":{"en":"We saw a wonder there, king: Shikhandi stood motionless in the battle, like stones afloat."}},{"n":12,"text":"कृपेण छादितं दृष्ट्वा नृपोत्तम शिखण्डिनम् ।\nप्रत्युद्ययौ कृपं तूर्णं धृष्टद्युम्नो महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of kings, seeing Shikhandi covered by Kripa, the great chariot-warrior Dhrishtadyumna quickly went against Kripa."}},{"n":13,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नं ततो यान्तं शारद्वतरथं प्रति ।\nप्रतिजग्राह वेगेन कृतवर्मा महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Dhrishtadyumna advanced against the chariot of Kripa, son of Sharadvan, the great chariot-warrior Kritavarma swiftly checked him."}},{"n":14,"text":"युधिष्ठिरमथायान्तं शारद्वतरथं प्रति ।\nसपुत्रं सहसेनं च द्रोणपुत्रो न्यवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Yudhishthira, as he came toward the chariot of Kripa, son of Sharadvan, was held back along with his son and army by Ashvatthama, son of Drona."}},{"n":15,"text":"नकुलं सहदेवं च त्वरमाणौ महारथौ ।\nप्रतिजग्राह ते पुत्रः शरवर्षेण वारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son Duryodhana, holding off the two great chariot-warriors Nakula and Sahadeva as they hurried on, checked them with a shower of arrows."}},{"n":16,"text":"भीमसेनं करूषांश्च केकयान्सहसृञ्जयान् ।\nकर्णो वैकर्तनो युद्धे वारयामास भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, Karna, son of Vikartana, held back in the battle Bhimasena, the Karushas, the Kekayas and the Srinjayas."}},{"n":17,"text":"शिखण्डिनस्ततो बाणान्कृपः शारद्वतो युधि ।\nप्राहिणोत्त्वरया युक्तो दिधक्षुरिव मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kripa, son of Sharadvan, eager in the fight, sent his arrows at Shikhandi as if wishing to burn him, lord."}},{"n":18,"text":"ताञ्शरान्प्रेषितांस्तेन समन्ताद्धेमभूषणान् ।\nचिच्छेद खड्गमाविध्य भ्रामयंश्च पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whirling his sword round and round, Shikhandi cut down those golden-adorned arrows that Kripa had sent from every side."}},{"n":19,"text":"शतचन्द्रं ततश्चर्म गौतमः पार्षतस्य ह ।\nव्यधमत्सायकैस्तूर्णं तत उच्चुक्रुशुर्जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kripa, son of Gautama, quickly destroyed with his arrows the shield of the son of Prishata, which was marked with a hundred moons, and people cried out."}},{"n":20,"text":"स विचर्मा महाराज खड्गपाणिरुपाद्रवत् ।\nकृपस्य वशमापन्नो मृत्योरास्यमिवातुरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, Shikhandi, now without a shield, sword in hand, ran forward, fallen into Kripa's power like a sick man into the jaws of death."}},{"n":21,"text":"शारद्वतशरैर्ग्रस्तं क्लिश्यमानं महाबलम् ।\nचित्रकेतुसुतो राजन्सुकेतुस्त्वरितो ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, as that mighty man was gripped and tormented by the arrows of Kripa, Suketu, son of Chitraketu, hurried to him."}},{"n":22,"text":"विकिरन्ब्राह्मणं युद्धे बहुभिर्निशितैः शरैः ।\nअभ्यापतदमेयात्मा गौतमस्य रथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Scattering many sharp arrows at the brahmin in the battle, that man of immeasurable spirit attacked Gautama's chariot."}},{"n":23,"text":"दृष्ट्वाविषह्यं तं युद्धे ब्राह्मणं चरितव्रतम् ।\nअपयातस्ततस्तूर्णं शिखण्डी राजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of kings, seeing that the brahmin who had kept his vows was too strong to resist, Shikhandi quickly withdrew."}},{"n":24,"text":"सुकेतुस्तु ततो राजन्गौतमं नवभिः शरैः ।\nविद्ध्वा विव्याध सप्तत्या पुनश्चैनं त्रिभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, Suketu then wounded Gautama with nine arrows, and again with seventy, and once more with three."}},{"n":25,"text":"अथास्य सशरं चापं पुनश्चिच्छेद मारिष ।\nसारथिं च शरेणास्य भृशं मर्मण्यताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord, he then cut Kripa's bow along with its arrow once again, and struck his charioteer badly in a vital spot with an arrow."}},{"n":26,"text":"गौतमस्तु ततः क्रुद्धो धनुर्गृह्य नवं दृढम् ।\nसुकेतुं त्रिंशता बाणैः सर्वमर्मस्वताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Gautama, angry, took up a new, strong bow and struck Suketu in all his vital parts with thirty arrows."}},{"n":27,"text":"स विह्वलितसर्वाङ्गः प्रचचाल रथोत्तमे ।\nभूमिचाले यथा वृक्षश्चलत्याकम्पितो भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With all his limbs shaken, Suketu trembled on his excellent chariot, as a tree shakes violently in an earthquake."}},{"n":28,"text":"चलतस्तस्य कायात्तु शिरो ज्वलितकुण्डलम् ।\nसोष्णीषं सशिरस्त्राणं क्षुरप्रेणान्वपातयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As his body shook, Kripa struck off with a razor-edged arrow his head with its blazing earrings, turban and helmet."}},{"n":29,"text":"तच्छिरः प्रापतद्भूमौ श्येनाहृतमिवामिषम् ।\nततोऽस्य कायो वसुधां पश्चात्प्राप तदा च्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That head fell to the ground like meat carried off by a hawk, and then the body, too, dropped to earth."}},{"n":30,"text":"तस्मिन्हते महाराज त्रस्तास्तस्य पदानुगाः ।\nगौतमं समरे त्यक्त्वा दुद्रुवुस्ते दिशो दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, when he was slain, his followers, terrified, left Gautama in the battle and ran off in all ten directions."}},{"n":31,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नं तु समरे संनिवार्य महाबलः ।\nकृतवर्माब्रवीद्धृष्टस्तिष्ठ तिष्ठेति पार्षतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty Kritavarma, having held back Dhrishtadyumna in the battle, cheerfully said to the son of Prishata, \"Stand, stand!\""}},{"n":32,"text":"तदभूत्तुमुलं युद्धं वृष्णिपार्षतयो रणे ।\nआमिषार्थे यथा युद्धं श्येनयोर्गृद्धयोर्नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, a tumultuous fight began in the battle between the Vrishni and the son of Prishata, like the fight of two hungry hawks over meat."}},{"n":33,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नस्तु समरे हार्दिक्यं नवभिः शरैः ।\nआजघानोरसि क्रुद्धः पीडयन्हृदिकात्मजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna, angry in the battle, struck Hridika's son Kritavarma in the chest with nine arrows, tormenting him."}},{"n":34,"text":"कृतवर्मा तु समरे पार्षतेन दृढाहतः ।\nपार्षतं सरथं साश्वं छादयामास सायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kritavarma, hard hit in the battle by the son of Prishata, covered Dhrishtadyumna together with his chariot and horses with arrows."}},{"n":35,"text":"सरथश्छादितो राजन्धृष्टद्युम्नो न दृश्यते ।\nमेघैरिव परिच्छन्नो भास्करो जलदागमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, Dhrishtadyumna, covered with his chariot, could no longer be seen, like the sun hidden by clouds when the rains come."}},{"n":36,"text":"विधूय तं बाणगणं शरैः कनकभूषणैः ।\nव्यरोचत रणे राजन्धृष्टद्युम्नः कृतव्रणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shaking off that mass of arrows with golden-adorned arrows of his own, Dhrishtadyumna, though wounded, shone in the battle, king."}},{"n":37,"text":"ततस्तु पार्षतः क्रुद्धः शस्त्रवृष्टिं सुदारुणाम् ।\nकृतवर्माणमासाद्य व्यसृजत्पृतनापतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the son of Prishata, the commander, angry, came up to Kritavarma and let loose a terrible shower of weapons."}},{"n":38,"text":"तामापतन्तीं सहसा शस्त्रवृष्टिं निरन्तराम् ।\nशरैरनेकसाहस्रैर्हार्दिक्यो व्यधमद्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Hridika destroyed in the fight, with many thousands of arrows, that dense shower of weapons as it rushed suddenly upon him."}},{"n":39,"text":"दृष्ट्वा तु दारितां युद्धे शस्त्रवृष्टिं दुरुत्तराम् ।\nकृतवर्माणमभ्येत्य वारयामास पार्षतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But seeing that hard-to-cross shower of weapons torn apart in the battle, the son of Prishata went up to Kritavarma and checked him."}},{"n":40,"text":"सारथिं चास्य तरसा प्राहिणोद्यमसादनम् ।\nभल्लेन शितधारेण स हतः प्रापतद्रथात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With a sharp-edged broad-headed arrow he quickly sent Kritavarma's charioteer to Yama's abode, and the charioteer, slain, fell from the chariot."}},{"n":41,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नस्तु बलवाञ्जित्वा शत्रुं महारथम् ।\nकौरवान्समरे तूर्णं वारयामास सायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty Dhrishtadyumna, having overcome that great chariot-warrior, his enemy, quickly held back the Kauravas in the battle with his arrows."}},{"n":42,"text":"ततस्ते तावका योधा धृष्टद्युम्नमुपाद्रवन् ।\nसिंहनादरवं कृत्वा ततो युद्धमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your warriors rushed upon Dhrishtadyumna with lion-roars, and the fighting went on."}}]}]}